WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:14.967
Bottom line: recommend sending a focused cross-functional team to Power Platform Community Conference 2026 with one objective: return with a governed AI, app, and automation pilot proposal.

00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.767
This is a recommendation, not a measured outcome.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:29.867
PPCC runs October 27 through 29 at the MGM Grand in Las Vegas, with separate workshops before and after the main conference.

00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:37.367
The timing matters because leaders need operating patterns, not another technology tour.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:49.933
Microsoft frames the agenda around Copilot, agents, apps, automation, and data, and says these elements can work together as complete, governed business solutions.

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:56.933
The conference FAQ adds real implementation, architecture, governance, and AI-driven scenarios.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:03.067
That combination can help a team connect innovation ambition to execution controls.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.400
Send business, platform, data, and risk leaders with a narrow brief.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:12.367
Capture the workflow, trusted data, and controls needed.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:19.533
After the event, ask for one pilot charter with an owner, guardrails, and a testable success measure.
